      {
        "id": 115851,
        "name": "DrScott",
        "username": "DrScott",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-22T01:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You remove all Auto-misses, then the rest of them become 6, as long as you rolled a 6.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That seemed to me to be the way to go, but the rule book states, \"You may spend an Aim token before making an attack to make all of the attack dice you roll equal the highest die you roll for one of your targets.\"</p>\n<p><em>Urg, just found it - under \"Actions for Everyone!\" it specifies \"after removing misses.\" &nbsp;Both the text under \"Effect Tokens\" and in the \"Glosser\" leave that part out entirely. &nbsp; I thought that was too powerful. &nbsp;I guess I didn't loose so badly after all.</em></p>\n<p><em>Actually, that's a pretty big rulebook oops. &nbsp;&nbsp;</em></p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:48:08.174Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11091,
        "topic_slug": "aim-snapshot-micromissles-am-i-playing-this-right",
        "display_username": "DrScott",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
